<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scalptūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A cutting</i>, <i>carving</i>, or <i>graving</i> in stone: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 7, 30, § 104</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 10</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 63, § 173</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Concr., <i>a graved
				figure</i>, <i>a sculpture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zophori scalpturis ornati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					4, 1, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 9, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">3, 3,
		10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
